From b53a620652d44dc3178587d90892b6123aa1fdf8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 23:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(core): retain decode-frontier SWA checkpoints and order
 hybrid KV eviction tail-to-root

Base: 1107 vLLM patch head 2756478b60b90700b9918b457aeb38657da637b5.

Rationale:
Multi-turn 64K-100K agent conversations with hybrid FullAttention (block_size=256) + SlidingWindow (block_size=128, window=128) KV cache and sparse prefix_cache_retention_interval (512 on tp3-triangle, 8192 on tp4-ring) lose prefix-cache hits in three places in vllm/v1/core/:
1. Decode-frontier SWA checkpoint loss: SparseRetentionPolicy._retain only retained segment multiples (k * interval) and prompt boundaries (request.num_prompt_tokens). During decode (num_tokens > request.num_prompt_tokens), whenever a turn stopped at T_end with T_end % 256 >= 128 on a non-segment boundary, SlidingWindowManager.remove_skipped_blocks freed the 128-token SWA block at floor(T_end / 256) * 256 un-hashed before free() ran, causing the next turn to miss the decoded 256-token boundary.
2. Group-major free order: KVCacheCoordinator.free freed every block of group 0 tail-to-root, then every block of group 1, and so on. When pool pressure reaches a finished conversation, it evicts one group's blocks position after position while the other groups' blocks at those positions stay cached but unusable, so each evicted block shortens the next hit by a whole 256-token page.
3. Un-cached boundary crossing on speculative decode stopping steps: Scheduler._update_request_with_output omitted kv_cache_manager.cache_blocks when a running request crossed a block boundary via accepted draft tokens on the same step that stopped the request, and AsyncScheduler._update_request_with_output lacked a staleness and num_tokens clamp guard.

Fix all three gaps:
- In SlidingWindowManager.cache_blocks, retain the active decode frontier (resend_lo, resend_hi, aligned_ext) SWA tail blocks across 256-token MLA boundaries while recycling obsolete intermediate non-segment decode-frontier SWA blocks (un-hashing and prepending to the scratch front of free_block_queue via prepend_n), leaving only the final turn endpoint SWA checkpoint cached at turn completion alongside sparse segment checkpoints.
- Sort KVCacheCoordinator.pop_blocks_for_free across groups by token position, so free() returns a finished request's blocks to the free queue strictly tail-to-root across all groups, with full-attention blocks evicted before SWA blocks at the same token position.
- SWA checkpoints that a later hit did not read keep their LRU age. A sliding-window hit reads only the window that ends at the hit (SlidingWindowManager.find_longest_cache_hit stops at the first cached window from the right), so evicting an older checkpoint never shortens an extension of the same conversation, while it does free a block before any live conversation tail.
- In Scheduler._update_request_with_output and AsyncScheduler._update_request_with_output, call kv_cache_manager.cache_blocks(request, min(request.num_computed_tokens, request.num_tokens)) whenever a non-stale running request advances num_computed_tokens with zero remaining output placeholders before freeing on stop.

Rework (candidate-48): the first revision also re-appended every retained SWA checkpoint of a matched prefix to the MRU end of free_block_queue on each hit, on each sliding-window advance and on free, and re-sorted a finished request's already-free checkpoints into one tail-to-root run. That moved the aged checkpoints, the pool's harmless first eviction victims, behind the live conversation tails, so pool pressure evicted a conversation's newest MLA and SWA blocks first: the stress probe's evicted turns lost up to 5,120 tokens each, and its overall reusable-prefix hit share fell to 99.38% (tp3) and 98.97% (tp4), below 1107's 99.68% and 99.54%. That refresh is removed; with it goes the per-request retained-checkpoint map and the per-block prefix-chain map it needed.

Quality:
Bit- and mathematically identical KV attention and compressor contents; no change to what a hit reads. Only which blocks stay hashed and the order in which free cached blocks are evicted change.

Tests:
- pytest tests/v1/core/test_prefix_cache_retention_probe.py tests/v1/core/test_prefix_group_validity.py tests/v1/core/prefix_cache/test_mamba_boundary_capture.py tests/v1/core/prefix_cache/test_mamba_boundary_capture_digest.py tests/v1/core/prefix_cache/test_mamba_eagle_resume_checkpoint.py tests/v1/core/prefix_cache/test_partial_prefix_cache_hits.py tests/v1/core/prefix_cache/test_partial_prefix_cache_primitives.py tests/v1/core/prefix_cache/test_sparse_event_context.py tests/v1/core/test_async_scheduler.py tests/v1/core/test_boundary_admission.py tests/v1/core/test_boundary_admission_aged_cache.py tests/v1/core/test_boundary_admission_continuation.py tests/v1/core/test_boundary_admission_horizon.py tests/v1/core/test_boundary_admission_review.py tests/v1/core/test_partial_attention_rewind.py tests/v1/core/test_prefix_caching.py tests/v1/core/test_single_type_kv_cache_manager.py tests/v1/core/test_sink_draft_zero.py tests/v1/core/test_swa_inflight_window_free.py tests/v1/worker/test_boundary_checkpoint_attention.py tests/v1/worker/test_boundary_checkpoint_restore_scalars.py tests/kernels/attention/test_deepseek_v41_ced_replay.py tests/v1/attention/test_b12x_v41_ced_metadata.py
- test_shared_block_pool_tail_to_root_eviction_order asserts the order above: aged SWA checkpoints first, then the finished request's blocks tail-to-root across groups, and an extension hit at the full tail after every aged checkpoint is evicted. The 64K-100K stress test asserts the exact 256-token boundary hit on every turn, evicted or not.

Upstream status: local fix for hybrid MLA + SWA sparse prefix-cache retention and eviction ordering.
